\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every invertible mixing transformation T preserving a probability measure, every integer $m>=2$ and bounded measurable $f_1,...,f_m$, do $(1/N)sum_{n=1}^N$ $product_{j=1}^m$ $f_j(T^{jn}x)$ converge for almost every x to $product_j$ integral $f_j$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every invertible mixing transformation T preserving a probability measure, every integer $m>=2$ and bounded measurable $f_1,...,f_m$, do $(1/N)sum_{n=1}^N$ $product_{j=1}^m$ $f_j(T^{jn}x)$ converge for almost every x to $product_j$ integral $f_j$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.3808}.
\item[S2] Original question source or mathematical context.
